# XBD 6.3 Wide-Character Codes
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# Run in the POSIX locale and in every locale `locale -a` lists.

assertion  XBD.6.3-wide-character-codes.001
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap06.html#6.3
class      required
since      1992
says       In the POSIX locale the wide-character code of each portable
           character equals its character constant, through btowc, mbrtowc,
           wcrtomb and wctob.
test       t/001-posix-code-equals-constant.c

assertion  XBD.6.3-wide-character-codes.002
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap06.html#6.3
class      required
since      1992
says       In every locale the wide codes of the portable letters, digits
           and white-space characters are their character constants: they
           lie in the classes the locale definition puts those characters
           in.
test       t/002-every-locale-classes.c

assertion  XBD.6.3-wide-character-codes.003
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap06.html#6.3
class      required
since      1992
says       The wide-character string and memory functions give array
           elements that are not valid wide codes of the locale their
           specified semantics (lengths, copies, comparisons, searches).
test       t/003-invalid-codes-in-strings.c
